# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IMPORTANT UNITY META RULE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Do NOT add a global rule such as "*.meta".
# Meta files belonging to published source files, such as .cs.meta,
# .asmdef.meta, and .inputactions.meta, should remain tracked so Unity GUIDs
# stay stable. Asset-specific .meta files are excluded above in pairs.
#
# Intended public files include, for example:
#   Assets/**/*.cs
#   Assets/**/*.cs.meta
#   Assets/**/*.asmdef
#   Assets/**/*.asmdef.meta
#   Assets/**/*.asmref
#   Assets/**/*.asmref.meta
#   Assets/**/*.inputactions
#   Assets/**/*.inputactions.meta
#   Packages/manifest.json
#   Packages/packages-lock.json
#   ProjectSettings/*.asset  (NOTE: currently excluded by *.asset)
#   README.md
#   LICENSE
#
# Because *.asset is ignored, Unity ProjectSettings files will also be ignored.
# This is deliberate for the safest source-only public repository. If specific
# ProjectSettings files are required, whitelist only reviewed files below.
# Example:
#   !/ProjectSettings/ProjectVersion.txt
# ============================================================================

# Safe, useful project metadata
!/ProjectSettings/
/ProjectSettings/*
!/ProjectSettings/ProjectVersion.txt
!/Packages/
!/Packages/manifest.json
!/Packages/packages-lock.json
